      "writtenOn": "2018-10-18T23:51:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Jett, \n\nInterrupt based(Tx FIFO threshold interrupt) implementation is for CPU does other task while data are transmitted to the slave device and when the transmission is done, i2c_Xfer driver resumes rest of work.  In current situation, as I mentioned above, waiting time for both Tx of 6 byte + preparing Rx is around 8 uSec and the implementation might be less efficient and I think small wait loop will be more efficient.   When we have a situation for sending big size data to slave device, then, we can revise driver later.  For Trackpad and sensors are all Rx data size is big but Tx(commands) are small.",
      "parentUuid": "cb5ffcbb_ecff4d55",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 336,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 336,
        "endChar": 41
